{"audit_run_id":"audit:d85b13f93b3749329e40c6a7cdfe7020","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":97,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"The data file is `soil_respiration.csv`. It holds the soil respiration survey from the grassland"},{"end_column":57,"end_line":4,"start_column":1,"start_line":4,"text":"warming experiment, collected across one summer morning."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"One row is **a single soil CO2 efflux reading taken at one collar inside one plot**. It is one"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"measurement point, not a plot summary. Each row also carries the soil temperature and soil moisture"},{"end_column":57,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"recorded at that same collar at the time of the reading."},{"end_column":68,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"- 10 experimental plots, each 2 m by 2 m (`P-101` through `P-110`)."},{"end_column":66,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"- 6 fixed collar positions inside every plot (`C1` through `C6`)."},{"end_column":77,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"- 6 readings per plot x 10 plots = **60 rows** of data, plus one header row."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"- Rows are ordered plot by plot, and within each plot by collar position, in collection order."},{"end_column":53,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"Warming was applied to whole plots. Of the 10 plots:"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"- **ambient** (5 plots: P-101, P-104, P-105, P-107, P-110): dummy heater frames, no heat applied."},{"end_column":24,"end_line":24,"start_column":3,"start_line":24,"text":"30 readings in total."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"- **warmed** (5 plots: P-102, P-103, P-106, P-108, P-109): active infrared heaters holding the soil"},{"end_column":63,"end_line":26,"start_column":3,"start_line":26,"text":"about 2 degrees Celsius above ambient. 30 readings in total."},{"end_column":81,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"Heater assignment was interleaved across the plot numbering rather than blocked."},{"end_column":40,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"| Column | Type | Units | Description |"},{"end_column":26,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":122,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"| `plot_code` | string | - | The plot the reading came from, `P-101` through `P-110`. Ten distinct values, 6 rows each. |"},{"end_column":114,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"| `warming_status` | string | - | Treatment of that plot, either `ambient` or `warmed`. Constant within a plot. |"},{"end_column":123,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"| `collar_position` | string | - | Which of the six fixed collars in that plot the reading came from, `C1` through `C6`. |"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"| `soil_temp_c` | float, 2 dp | degrees Celsius | Soil temperature at 5 cm depth at that collar. |"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"| `soil_moisture_pct` | float, 1 dp | percent | Volumetric water content at that collar. |"},{"end_column":143,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"| `co2_efflux` | float, 2 dp | micromoles CO2 per square metre per second | Soil CO2 efflux at that collar. This is the outcome of interest. |"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":43,"start_column":1,"start_line":43,"text":"Plots differ from one another for reasons that have nothing to do with the heaters, such as soil"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"depth, root density, drainage, and microtopography. Because of that, the six collars inside one plot"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"give readings that are similar to each other, and the plot-to-plot spread in baseline efflux is at"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"least as large as the average difference between warmed and ambient plots. There are no missing"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"values in the file."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"The file was produced by `make_data.py` with a fixed random seed (20260821), so re-running that"},{"end_column":35,"end_line":50,"start_column":1,"start_line":50,"text":"script reproduces the CSV exactly."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:cdbb23cf8a517c15cf66","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.19.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:c0734399121030f657a0576ce19e32fe9b7cb3392c3a86e153599c3f43b740a5","end_line":50,"locator":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md:1-50","path":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
{"audit_run_id":"audit:d85b13f93b3749329e40c6a7cdfe7020","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":90,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Compare `co2_efflux` between the two levels of `warming_status` (`ambient` and `warmed`)."},{"end_column":93,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"The independent experimental unit is the plot. The column `plot_code` carries the value that"},{"end_column":151,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"identifies it: each plot has one distinct `plot_code` value. Warming was applied to whole plots, so the plot is the unit that was assigned to a group."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"The analysis is a two-group comparison of `co2_efflux` between the two levels of `warming_status`."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"This protocol does not select, require, or exclude any particular statistical procedure."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:2057b1895ab0fcfb1067","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.19.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:6a2d80b0ff76ed329e885744498f9b599b92fb176958d0381270af5f2c427a99","end_line":15,"locator":"PROTOCOL.md:1-15","path":"PROTOCOL.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
