{"audit_run_id":"audit:d85b13f93b3749329e40c6a7cdfe7020","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":95,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"All results below come from `soil_respiration.csv`. The file has 60 data rows plus a header. A"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"single row is one soil CO2 efflux reading taken at one collar inside one plot, together with the"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"soil temperature and soil moisture recorded at that same collar at the moment of the reading. A row"},{"end_column":66,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"is therefore an individual measurement point, not a plot average."},{"end_column":26,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"The file has six columns:"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"- `plot_code` — the plot the reading came from, coded `P-101` through `P-110` (ten plots, six rows"},{"end_column":9,"end_line":13,"start_column":3,"start_line":13,"text":"each)."},{"end_column":79,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"- `warming_status` — the treatment of that plot, either `ambient` or `warmed`."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"- `collar_position` — which of the six fixed collars in the plot produced the reading, `C1` through"},{"end_column":8,"end_line":16,"start_column":3,"start_line":16,"text":"`C6`."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"- `soil_temp_c` — soil temperature at 5 cm depth at that collar, in degrees Celsius."},{"end_column":82,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"- `soil_moisture_pct` — volumetric water content at that collar, as a percentage."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"- `co2_efflux` — soil CO2 efflux at that collar, in micromoles of CO2 per square metre per second."},{"end_column":33,"end_line":20,"start_column":3,"start_line":20,"text":"This is the response variable."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"Rows are ordered plot by plot, and within each plot by collar position, in the order they were"},{"end_column":40,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"collected. There are no missing values."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"The experiment is a grassland warming study with ten plots, each 2 m by 2 m. Five plots (P-102,"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"P-103, P-106, P-108, P-109) carry active infrared heaters that hold the soil roughly 2 degrees"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"Celsius above ambient. The other five (P-101, P-104, P-105, P-107, P-110) carry dummy heater frames"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"and act as controls. Heater assignment is interleaved across the plot numbering rather than blocked."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"Six fixed collars were installed in every plot, and the technician read all six collars in every"},{"end_column":62,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"plot on the same summer morning, giving 60 readings in total."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"The heaters performed as intended. Mean soil temperature at 5 cm was 20.04 degrees Celsius in the"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"warmed plots against 17.93 degrees Celsius in the controls, a gap of 2.11 degrees. Mean soil"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"moisture was similar in the two conditions, 22.1 percent under warming and 23.3 percent under"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"ambient conditions."},{"end_column":94,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"I compared soil CO2 efflux between the warmed and ambient conditions with a two-sample t-test"},{"end_column":63,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"(`scipy.stats.ttest_ind`, two-sided, equal variances assumed)."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"The measurements that entered the test were the individual collar readings from the `co2_efflux`"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"column. Every reading from a warmed plot was placed in the warmed sample and every reading from an"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"ambient plot was placed in the ambient sample. No averaging or aggregation was applied before the"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"test, and no readings were excluded. The sample sizes I am claiming are therefore **N = 30 readings"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":48,"start_column":1,"start_line":48,"text":"in the warmed condition and N = 30 readings in the ambient condition, 60 readings in total**, which"},{"end_column":29,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"gives 58 degrees of freedom."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":53,"start_column":1,"start_line":53,"text":"Soil CO2 efflux was higher under warming. The warmed condition averaged 3.19 micromoles of CO2 per"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":54,"start_column":1,"start_line":54,"text":"square metre per second (SD 0.83, N = 30 readings), and the ambient condition averaged 2.62"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":55,"start_column":1,"start_line":55,"text":"micromoles per square metre per second (SD 0.38, N = 30 readings). The difference between the two"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":56,"start_column":1,"start_line":56,"text":"means is 0.57 micromoles per square metre per second, an increase of about 22 percent over the"},{"end_column":15,"end_line":57,"start_column":1,"start_line":57,"text":"control level."},{"end_column":69,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"The t-test gives t = 3.44 with 58 degrees of freedom and p = 0.0011."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":63,"start_column":1,"start_line":63,"text":"Warming the soil by roughly 2 degrees Celsius raised soil CO2 efflux by about 0.57 micromoles of"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":64,"start_column":1,"start_line":64,"text":"CO2 per square metre per second relative to unheated controls, and the difference is statistically"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":65,"start_column":1,"start_line":65,"text":"significant at p = 0.0011. The result is consistent with a direct temperature stimulation of soil"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":66,"start_column":1,"start_line":66,"text":"respiration in this grassland, and the similar moisture levels in the two conditions indicate that"},{"end_column":64,"end_line":67,"start_column":1,"start_line":67,"text":"the effect is not driven by a difference in soil water content."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:b32562a8714f22dfa378","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.19.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:56eeaf954c930c199cc5c9751febc41c33a16a2f6c452263152c6d5c121f6d38","end_line":67,"locator":"report.md:1-67","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
